# TECH_STACK.md
## INTERIO – Interior Design & Renovation Cost Estimation Web App

---

## 1. Overview

This is the stack the project is built with. The first plan used Next.js, Express, Prisma and NextAuth; it was
changed to React + Vite on the frontend and Django on the backend, which gave an admin panel, ORM, migrations
and auth out of the box. The table at the end maps the original plan to what is used now.

Goals stayed the same:
- Fast development for a small team
- Free or near-free hosting
- Transparent, admin-editable pricing
- Lead generation for the studio

---

## 2. Frontend (`frontend/`)

| Purpose            | Choice                                                         |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Framework          | React 18 + TypeScript, built with Vite                         |
| Routing            | React Router 6 (pages load on demand)                          |
| Server data        | TanStack Query (caching, retries, live estimate preview)       |
| Styling            | Tailwind CSS with warm design tokens in `src/index.css`        |
| UI primitives      | Radix UI (dialog, select, dropdown, tooltip, ...)              |
| Icons              | Custom SVG set in `src/components/icons.tsx`                   |
| Animation          | framer-motion (respects the OS "reduce motion" setting)        |
| Notifications      | sonner toasts                                                  |
| Tests              | Vitest + Testing Library (jsdom)                               |
| Code quality       | ESLint + Prettier                                              |

Responsibilities: landing and marketing pages, the 6-step estimate wizard, package comparison, design gallery,
customer dashboard, staff panel, shared estimate pages.

