## 3. Backend (`backend/`)

| Purpose            | Choice                                                         |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Framework          | Django 5.2 + Django REST Framework                             |
| Auth               | Simple JWT (access + refresh tokens, blacklist on logout)      |
| Admin panel        | Django admin (pricing, catalog, designs, leads)                |
| PDF quotations     | ReportLab                                                      |
| Email              | Django email (SMTP, or printed to the console in development)   |
| CORS               | django-cors-headers                                            |
| Static files       | WhiteNoise                                                     |
| App server         | gunicorn                                                       |
| Tests              | Django TestCase + DRF APIClient                                |

Responsibilities: cost estimation engine (`api/pricing.py`), packages and pricing, furniture and renovation
options, saved estimates and share links, PDF quotations, consultations, contact messages, staff APIs,
email notifications, authentication.

---

## 4. Database

- **SQLite** in development (no setup needed)
- **PostgreSQL** in production through `DATABASE_URL` (Neon, Supabase or any host)
- Schema managed with Django migrations; default catalog loaded with `python manage.py seed`

Data: packages, rates, furniture, services, city multipliers, users and profiles, estimates (with a stored
snapshot of the result), gallery designs, saved designs, consultations, contact messages.

---

## 5. Authentication & Authorization

- Email + password sign up and sign in
- JWT access token (60 min) and single-use refresh token (7 days)
- Logout and password change revoke refresh tokens
- Roles: customer, and staff (`is_staff`) for the staff panel and Django admin
- Rate limiting on login, signup, password reset and the contact form

---

## 6. Cost Estimation Engine

Rule-based, every rate editable in the admin:

```
base      = carpet area × package rate per sq.ft
furniture = Σ item price × quantity × package furniture multiplier
services  = Σ per-sq.ft services × area + Σ per-unit services × quantity
subtotal  = base + furniture + services
total     = subtotal × city multiplier + 18% GST   (range shown as ±10%)
```

